#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The World in One Day - Wednesday 25 November 2026.

One newspaper front page summing up the world's news of Wednesday
25 November 2026: 40 verified stories, 13 of them highlighted with a
small drawn picture each, a world map with a numbered pin for every
story, a UTC timeline, stat boxes, and an honest date check.

Python 3.13, standard library only (os, struct, sys, zlib).  The
typefaces - Playfair Display Bold for the masthead and headlines,
Liberation Serif for body copy, Liberation Sans Bold for labels - are
baked in below as 4-bit grayscale coverage bitmaps, rendered from the
font files at build time with Pillow.  At run time this program only
decodes those bitmaps and blits them onto an RGB buffer, then encodes
the PNG by hand.  No network, no timestamps, no randomness: two runs
write byte-identical files.

Page plan (1024 x 1024, black and white with a sparing gold accent):
top band, masthead, kicker line, UTC timeline strip, stat boxes,
region bar, 13 highlight cards (3 large, 10 small), the world map
beside the 27 further stories, a DATE CHECK box and a HOW WE CHECKED
footer.  Every text box is measured from wrapped text, and the draw
records every text box in TRACE so a separate audit script can prove
nothing overflows its box and nothing sits near the page edge.
"""

